Previous publications showed that directly performing PCA on single-cell data may capture unwanted noise [80]. Therefore, bulk-supervised PCA were conducted to investigate differences between different cell types in the following manner. Denote the normalized bulk RNA-seq expression of gene g in sample s as Ygs. Prior to PCA analysis, for each gene g, the bulk RNA-seq expression values were rescaled to values with mean 0 and standard deviation 1 (denote as Ỹgs). Similarly, denote normalized scRNA-seq expression of gene g in cell j as Xgj and denote the rescaled data as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
